/x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/transforms/ClientTransformIndexer.java#L602\r\n\r\nI haven\u0027t seen this same type of intermittent failure scenario though, where the source index gets relocated to a new shard and the request fails on the old shard, so I\u0027m not sure if we just haven\u0027t seen it yet or if search behaves differently where the request will automatically reroute.","\u003e I\u0027m not sure if we just haven\u0027t seen it yet or if search behaves differently where the request will automatically reroute.\r\n\r\nI don\u0027t know either unfortunately :(\r\nBut since we are going in a direction to make more errors recoverable (and more transforms unattended) it could make sense to make `IndexNotFoundException` recoverable.\r\nBut maybe let\u0027s not do it in this PR if you don\u0027t feel comfortable.\r\nWe can leave this PR for dealing with destination index only.\r\nPlease make it clear in the PR title/description."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java","id":37106,"created_at":"2024-05-09T11:29:00Z","original_position":13,"side":"RIGHT","position":13,"submitted_on_commit":"1211b0a783364942412f5a3aeaea4167a51dd6e2","diff_hunk":"@@ -63,7 +64,7 @@ public static Throwable getFirstIrrecoverableExceptionFromBulkResponses(Collecti\n             }\n \n             if (unwrappedThrowable instanceof ElasticsearchException elasticsearchException) {\n-                if (isExceptionIrrecoverable(elasticsearchException)) {\n+                if (isExceptionIrrecoverable(elasticsearchException) \u0026\u0026 isNotIndexNotFoundException(elasticsearchException)) {","submitted_line":67},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The addition of `isNotIndexNotFoundException` method is logical. Ensure that this change does not alter the behavior of existing irrecoverable exception checks and that it aligns with the intended recovery strategy for `IndexNotFoundException`.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java-x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java-2432:2480-2487:2590","promptId":"#NCBCY","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":2432,"endPos":2480,"startLine":66,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":66,"endLineOffset":68,"length":49}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2487,"endPos":2590,"startLine":67,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":67,"endLineOffset":123,"length":104}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinderTests.java-x-pack/plugin/transform/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinderTests.java--5145:5257","promptId":"#AZDFM","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinderTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinderTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5145,"endPos":5257,"startLine":97,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":97,"endLineOffset":120,"length":113}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java-x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java--2720:3169","promptId":"#SVGX8","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2720,"endPos":3169,"startLine":7